# Crop Mutation Tree
This chart shows how crops relate to one another. Higher tiers are reached by treating
a plant with [color=cyan]unstable mutagen[/color] (or, in a few cases, by cross-pollination)
until it mutates into the next variety. Mutations flow from [bold]left to right[/bold]:
a crop in an earlier tier can mutate into the crops to its right on the same line.

Use this as a roadmap for what to grow once you have the basics covered. See the
[textlink="Botany" link="Botany"] page for how mutation and cross-pollination actually work.

## Legend
<Table Columns="5">
  <ColorBox Color="#6f9fd6" Margin="1"><Box Margin="3">Tier 1 — Basic</Box></ColorBox>
